%% Trusted tenant HTTP request lifecycle
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Browser
    participant BFF as Next.js BFF/SSR
    participant API as NestJS API
    participant Middleware as TenantContextMiddleware
    participant Resolver as TenantResolverService
    participant Redis
    participant Control as Control-plane DB
    participant Context as AsyncLocalStorage context
    participant Manager as TenantDatabaseManager
    participant Tenant as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Service as Feature service

    Browser->>BFF: Request on tenant.example
    BFF->>API: Forward request with trusted x-forwarded-host
    API->>Middleware: Run tenant middleware
    Middleware->>Resolver: Resolve effective host
    Resolver->>Resolver: Normalize host and validate trusted proxy chain
    Resolver->>Redis: Read positive or negative host cache

    alt Cache miss
        Resolver->>Control: Lookup active domain, organization, registry
        Control-->>Resolver: Organization and READY database metadata
        Resolver->>Redis: Cache bounded host result
    else Cache hit
        Redis-->>Resolver: Cached tenant registry result
    end

    Resolver->>Resolver: Reject unknown, inactive, suspended-write, or unavailable state
    Resolver->>Context: Store immutable tenant context
    Middleware->>Service: Continue request
    Service->>Manager: Get client from resolved context
    Manager->>Tenant: Acquire bounded tenant Prisma client
    Tenant-->>Service: Tenant-scoped data
    Service-->>API: Domain result or stable domain error
    API-->>BFF: Transformed response
    BFF-->>Browser: Tenant-safe response

    Note over Resolver: Browser input never selects a database.
    Note over Manager: Missing context fails loudly; no legacy fallback.
